{"timestamp":"2026-09-11T11:32:28.279Z","ordinal":2350,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0903d-8df7-7d30-aaf6-6e69e30b546f","call_id":"call_JNpTch3DqEFaUtzpIrQvutDn","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12832)\nTotal output lines: 3\n\n{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"2549ad\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002816,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":5994,\"output\":\"            # Raw KV on a SEPARATE load_kv_stream (the default; KV_H2D_ON_WEIGHT\\n            # aliases only the kvcomp path).  On the shared C2C link the per-\\n            # stream begin/end_memcpy_kv bracket fires at STREAM-queue position\\n            # while the engine is still draining the prefetched weight, so it\\n            # ABSORBS that weight (KVLoad >> real — the dirty artifact).  Do NOT\\n            # trust that bracket as a standalone value.  Recover the clean KV\\n            # engine-time as  engine_busy_union − weight :\\n            #   • the UNION of weight ∪ KV intervals is INFLATION-IMMUNE — the\\n            #     absorbed weight is double-counted (it lives in both the inflated\\n            #     KV interval AND the clean weight intervals), and the union-merge\\n            #     cancels that overlap → the union equals the true H2D engine-busy\\n            #     span (validated disjoint vs the nsys copy-engine timeline).\\n            #   • weight_load_time is the CLEAN head-of-queue weight union (weight\\n            #     is prefetched first, never queued behind KV → never absorbed).\\n            # KVLoad = union − weight is then exact, additive by construction\\n            # (WLoad+KVLoad = union ≤ GPUFwd), zero schedule perturbation (pure\\n            # post-hoc arithmetic on the fast baseline's recorded events), and a\\n            # real measurement (a genuine KV slowdow